[I] Manage installation of multiple softwares in the same directory tree

[T] GNU Stow is a symlink farm manager which takes distinct sets of software
[T] and/or data located in separate directories and makes them all appear to
[T] be installed in a single directory tree. It is used to manage software
[T] in /usr/local as well as dotfiles in home directories.

[U] https://www.gnu.org/software/stow/

[A] Stow Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

